.TH ISOTONE 1 "2026-09-19" "Isotone 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
isotone \- system-wide parametric equaliser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B isotone
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B isotone
is the Isotone window: parametric bands with a response graph and a live
spectrum, per-channel bands, speaker setup, and presets.
.PP
It edits the state of one output at a time. The audio itself is processed by
.BR isotone-daemon (1),
which the app offers to start when it is not running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-tray
Start hidden in the notification area. This is what the launch-at-sign-in entry
uses.
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-dir " directory"
Read and write presets and settings here instead of
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/isotone/ui .
.TP
.B \-\-first\-run
Show the first-run screens whether or not they have been finished before.
.TP
.B \-\-help
List every option, including the ones used for screenshots and testing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/isotone/ui
Presets and settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/isotone
Each sink's saved state, shared with the daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR isotone-daemon (1),
.BR isotone-state (1)
